                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_413\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (\"Add block/position convention to all distinct from operators\") adds a second, more efficient block/position-based implementation of the IS_DISTINCT_FROM operator to nearly every type in the codebase (Array, Map, Row, Json, Bigint, Boolean, Char, Color, Date, Double, Integer, IntervalDayTime, IntervalYearMonth, IpAddress, Real, Smallint, Time, TimeWithTimeZone, Timestamp, TimestampWithTimeZone, Tinyint, Unknown, Varbinary, Varchar), replacing/supplementing the original NULL_FLAG-convention implementation. In the original implementation (e.g. in ArrayDistinctFromOperator), each element's native value had to be extracted out of the Block via `TypeUtils.readNativeValue(type, block, i)`, with nulls substituted by `Defaults.defaultValue(type.getJavaType())`, and then passed by value (with a boolean null-flag) into the invoked MethodHandle. This is the exact \"performance issue\" described in the fix commit message: extracting values out of Blocks (boxing/copying) instead of operating directly on Block+position pairs.\n\ncandidate_413 is the commit that originally introduced this NULL_FLAG-convention IS_DISTINCT_FROM operator implementation for virtually all these types simultaneously: it adds new files ArrayDistinctFromOperator.java, MapDistinctFromOperator.java, MapGenericEquality.java, and RowDistinctFromOperator.java, adds isDistinctFrom methods to BigintOperators, BooleanOperators, CharOperators, ColorOperators, DateOperators, DoubleOperators, IntegerOperators, IntervalDayTimeOperators, IntervalYearMonthOperators, RealOperators, SmallintOperators, TimeOperators, TimeWithTimeZoneOperators, TimestampOperators, TimestampWithTimeZoneOperators, TinyintOperators, UnknownOperators, VarbinaryOperators, and VarcharOperators \u2014 using precisely the readNativeValue/defaultValue/function.invoke pattern that the fix commit later replaces with block-position access (function.invokeExact(block, position, ...)).\n\nSince candidate_413 is the first commit (in chronological order among the 578 candidates) to introduce this inefficient value-extraction pattern for the IS_DISTINCT_FROM operator across the codebase \u2014 the exact code being reworked by the fix commit \u2014 it is the bug (performance-issue)-introducing commit.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
